description:
Design a frequency divider that takes a 100 MHz clock input and generates a 1 Hz output clock. The module counts the clock cycles of the 100 MHz signal and toggles the output frequency when it reaches 50 million cycles, effectively creating a signal that toggles every second.
module top_module(
    input C_100Mhz,
    output reg C_1Hz  // Change C_1Hz to reg type
);

code:
module top_module(
    input C_100Mhz,
    output reg C_1Hz  // Change C_1Hz to reg type
);reg [31:0] contador = 0; 

    always @(posedge C_100Mhz) 
    begin 
        if (contador == 50000000-1) 
        begin 
            C_1Hz <= ~C_1Hz; 
            contador <= 0; 
        end 
        else 
        begin 
            contador <= contador + 1; 
        end 
    end 
endmodule

