description:
Design a clock delay buffer that introduces a delay of a specified number of clock cycles (default is 4 cycles) to the input clock signal. Upon receiving a reset signal, the output clock is set to LOW, and the delay register is reset. On each rising edge of the clock, the module shifts the current clock value through a series of internal registers, ultimately driving the output clock (CLK_OUT) with the value from the last stage of the delay line, thereby providing a delayed version of the input clock signal.
module top_module(
    input CLK, RST,
    output reg CLK_OUT
);

code:
module top_module(
    input CLK, RST,
    output reg CLK_OUT
);parameter DELAY_CYCLES = 4;
    reg [DELAY_CYCLES-1:0] delay_reg;
    integer i;

    always @(posedge CLK or posedge RST) begin
        if (RST) begin
            CLK_OUT <= 0;
            delay_reg <= 0;
        end else begin
            delay_reg[0] <= CLK;
            for (i = 1; i < DELAY_CYCLES; i = i+1) begin
                delay_reg[i] <= delay_reg[i-1];
            end
            CLK_OUT <= delay_reg[DELAY_CYCLES-1];
        end
    end

endmodule

