description:
Design a three-stage pipeline for a one-bit XOR operation. The module takes two inputs, a and b, and computes the XOR of these inputs in a staged manner. The result is passed through two intermediate registers before being output. Each stage captures the output of the previous stage, effectively implementing a pipelining technique that can be beneficial in synchronous designs, allowing for improved timing and potential throughput in a larger system.
module top_module(
    input a,
    input b,
    output reg out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input a,
    input b,
    output reg out
);reg stage1_out;
reg stage2_out;

always @ (a, b) begin
    stage1_out <= a ^ b;
end

always @ (stage1_out) begin
    stage2_out <= stage1_out;
end

always @ (stage2_out) begin
    out <= stage2_out;
end

endmodule

