Design a circuit that performs a series of operations on a 32-bit input to produce a 64-bit output. The module first left-shifts the input value by 4 bits, effectively appending four zeros, then adds a fixed 64-bit value (0x12345678) to the shifted input. Lastly, the result of this addition is XORed with a predefined constant key (0x0123456789ABCDEF) to generate the final output. This module can be utilized for cryptographic or data transformation applications requiring bit manipulation and obfuscation.
module top_module(
	input [31:0] in,
	output [63:0] out
);

