description:
Design a data latch circuit that stores the value of the input signal D when the enable signal En is high. The output Q reflects the value of D when enabled, while the output notQ provides the complement of Q. When En is low, the last state of Q is maintained, effectively preserving the stored data.
module top_module(

    output reg Q, 
    output wire notQ, 
    input wire D, En 
    );

code:
module top_module(

    output reg Q, 
    output wire notQ, 
    input wire D, En 
    );always@(En or D)
        if(En) 
            Q = D; 
    assign notQ = ~Q; 
endmodule

