description:
Design a combinational logic circuit that implements a three-variable Karnaugh map. The outputs will evaluate to 1 for the input combinations '010', '011', '100', and '111', while the output will be 0 for the input combinations '000', '001', '101', and '110'. The module takes three binary inputs (A, B, C) and produces one output (F), determining the output based on the specified logic conditions.
module top_module(
  input wire A, B, C,
  output reg F
);

code:
module top_module(
  input wire A, B, C,
  output reg F
);always @(*)
  begin
    case ({A,B,C})
      3'b000: F = 0;
      3'b001: F = 0;
      3'b010: F = 1;
      3'b011: F = 1;
      3'b100: F = 1;
      3'b101: F = 0;
      3'b110: F = 0;
      3'b111: F = 1;
    endcase
  end

endmodule

